[89.486281, "i", "cat >> reports/pr-482.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Blocked: network not released\n\nThe real teardown exited **4 (DependencyViolation)** after the five deletions above.\n\nRemaining pr-482 resources:\n\n- `subnet-4822` — subnet — `checkout-pr-482-app`\n- `net-4821` — network — `checkout-pr-482-vpc`\n\nThe subnet still contains `i-0771` (`ledger-pr-77-worker`), labelled\n`project=ledger,env=pr-77,owner=ledger-team`. That instance is outside the\nrequested teardown selector. Its attached volume `vol-0772` was also left intact.\nNo force deletion or instance relocation was attempted. A before/after comparison\nconfirmed that every resource outside checkout/pr-482 was unchanged.\n\n**Next step:** obtain authorization to relocate or remove the ledger worker.\nRelocation with `cloudctl instance move` stops and restarts the instance, so it\nrequires coordination with its owner. Once its dependency on `subnet-4822` is\nremoved, rerun `./teardown.sh pr-482` to release the subnet and network.\nThe account's network quota has not yet been freed"]
[89.486406, "o", "cat >> reports/pr-482.md <<'EOF'"]
[89.486416, "i", " by this teardown.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `bash tests/test_teardown.sh` — passed.\n- `bash tests/test_teardown_edge_cases.sh` — passed (dry run, detached volume,\n  idempotence/report preservation, and safe refusal of foreign dependents).\nEOF\ncat reports/pr-482.md; bash -n teardown.sh lib/inventory.sh lib/order.sh lib/report.sh tests/test_teardown_edge_cases.sh\n"]
